      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Who owns Imperial Commercial Cooking Equipment?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Imperial is part of Middleby Corporation's family of foodservice brands (per imperialrange.com — 'Now a proud member of Middleby Corporation's family of foodservice brands'). Founded 1957 in Los Angeles, Imperial manufactures in Corona, California today — and that California factory remains operational under the Middleby umbrella. That combination — Middleby parent scale plus California-retained manufacturing — is structurally rare, since most Middleby acquisitions consolidate to the Winston-Salem distribution. Sibling Middleby brands include Pitco and Frymaster fryers, Blodgett deck and conveyor ovens, TurboChef rapid cook, and Wells built-in cooking. For LA operators running multi-Middleby kitchens, single SDAR service account covers the full sibling list."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Corona California parts advantage — what does that mean operationally?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Imperial parts ship direct from the Corona, California factory with 1 to 3 business day typical lead times to LA. Same-day pickup is possible for our SFV/LA-proper service area when timing matters. Compare to Hobart parts from Troy OH (3 to 5 days), Vulcan parts from Chicago distribution (3 to 5 days), Frymaster parts from Shreveport LA (3 to 5 days), Pitco parts from Bow NH (5 to 7 days), and Chinese OEM value-tier alternatives at 5 to 10 days via WebstaurantStore or Restaurant Depot. The Corona proximity is a structural advantage specific to LA-area Imperial operators and compounds with the Middleby family scale on national-distribution components."
        }
