<!-- ── CALIFORNIA TRIO ── -->
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow-sub">California local-manufacturer trio</p>
    <h2>Imperial + American Range + Montague — California manufacturing across consolidator parents</h2>
    <p>Three California-manufactured commercial cooking brands cluster on the LA service map with parts-chain advantages over national-brand competitors. Each has a different parent corporation today, but all three keep California manufacturing operational — making the trio a structural California-proximity advantage for LA operators regardless of parent-corp identity.</p>
    <p><strong>Imperial Range</strong> (Corona CA, 60 miles from LA) — this page's brand; Middleby Corporation family with California factory retained.</p>
    <p><strong>American Range</strong> (Pacoima CA, 15-20 miles from LA, San Fernando Valley) — Hatco Corporation family since October 2022 with California factory retained; see our <a href="/brands/american-range-repair/">American Range repair page</a> for the equivalent brand coverage.</p>
    <p><strong>Montague</strong> (Hayward CA, 360 miles but California-based) — Ali Group since July 2022 with California manufacturing continuity; see our <a href="/brands/montague-oven-repair/">Montague oven repair page</a>.</p>
    <p>The California trio shares a structural parts-lead-time advantage over national-brand competitors. Parent-corp mix across the trio is now diverse — Imperial is Middleby family, American Range is Hatco family, Montague is Ali Group — but all three keep California manufacturing as the defining LA-service operational advantage regardless of consolidator parent identity. For LA operators evaluating commercial cooking brand options, the California trio's combined coverage gives meaningful flexibility on equipment specification while preserving parts-proximity economics.</p>
  </div>
